# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Leatherworking --out` from Forever's client tables, trainer lists and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/leatherworking
title Leatherworking 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Leatherworking turns the leather and hides that Skinning gives into armor kits, leather and mail
# armour, quivers and ammo pouches, and cures hides with Salt. Skinning is its partner. Thread, Salt
# and dyes come from leatherworking and trade supplies vendors.
#
# Forever's changes: nearly every pattern moved 25 points down: trainers teach it 25 points earlier
# (Embossed Leather Gloves at 40, Fine Leather Belt at 55, Heavy Leather at 125) and it greys 25
# points sooner. Spell 2167 is now Gray Leather Boots; Forever's Dark Leather Boots is a new pattern
# at 35. Many 125-225 patterns, Cured Rugged Hide and the specialisation patterns need a Tanning
# Rack, a camp station from a blueprint Razorclaw the Butcher drops in Shadowfang Keep; no town has
# one, so this route leaves them out. The 270+ dungeon patterns need a Sewing Machine (no known
# blueprint source). New stat sets and the Forceful Thick Armor Kit are sold for Merchant's Favor by
# Pawani near the Crossroads and Daniel Stitchsong at Three Corners (Redridge). Merchant's Favor is
# a currency from the supply crates turned in at the camps, not gold; its patterns bind when picked
# up.
#
# Camping: Camp Tent (skill 20, 5 Light Leather) is the Leatherworking camp item and still gives
# points until 25. Tanning Rack (125 since Forever's 2026-11-06 hotfixes) and Sewing Machine (300)
# as above.
#
# Ranks: Journeyman needs character level 10 (Forever's sniffed lists). Trainers teach by tier and
# train only from their tier's skill: Journeyman at the city trainers, from skill 50; Expert only at
# Telonis (Darnassus) and Una (Thunder Bluff), from 125; Artisan only at Drakk Stonehand (Aerie
# Peak, the Hinterlands) and Hahrana Ironhide (Camp Mojache, Feralas), from 200. Specialisation at
# 225 and level 40: Dragonscale (Peter Galen, Azshara / Thorkaf Dragoneye, Badlands), Elemental
# (Sarah Tanner, Searing Gorge / Brumn Winterhoof, Arathi Highlands) or Tribal (at 235: Caryssia
# Moonhunter, Feralas / Se'Jib, Stranglethorn Vale).
#
# Route (crafts are expected counts; yellow and green crafts can take more):
#     1-51  Light Armor Kit, about 64 (known): 1 Light Leather each
#    51-75  Embossed Leather Gloves, about 25 (trainer 1s 50c): 3 Light Leather and 2 Coarse Thread each
#    75-102 Fine Leather Belt, about 35 (trainer 3s): 6 Light Leather and 2 Coarse Thread each
#   102-125 Nimble Leather Gloves, about 24 (trainer 5s): 1 Elixir of Minor Agility, 6 Medium Leather and 1 Fine Thread each
#   125-150 Heavy Armor Kit, about 26 (trainer 7s 50c): 5 Heavy Leather and 1 Fine Thread each
#   150-158 Heavy Armor Kit, about 15 (trainer 7s 50c): 5 Heavy Leather and 1 Fine Thread each
#   158-165 Barbaric Shoulders, about 7 (trainer): 8 Heavy Leather, 1 Cured Heavy Hide and 2 Fine Thread each
#   165-180 Guardian Gloves, about 15 (trainer): 4 Heavy Leather, 1 Cured Heavy Hide and 1 Silken Thread each
#   180-213 Nightscape Headband, about 41 (trainer): 5 Thick Leather and 2 Silken Thread each
#   213-225 Nightscape Pants, about 12 (trainer): 14 Thick Leather and 4 Silken Thread each
#   225-239 Rugged Armor Kit, about 23 (trainer): 5 Rugged Leather each
#   239-269 Wicked Leather Gauntlets, about 39 (recipe 1g 20s): 8 Rugged Leather, 1 Black Dye and 1 Rune Thread each
#   269-300 Runic Leather Headband, about 43 (recipe 2g 20s): 14 Rugged Leather, 10 Runecloth and 1 Rune Thread each
#
# Shopping per bracket (vendor goods at vendor prices; gathered or dropped materials by count):
# 1-75: Apprentice 10c, recipes 1s 50c, vendor goods 5s; gather or buy 349 Light Leather.
# 75-150: Journeyman 5s, recipes 15s 50c, vendor goods 57s; gather or buy 144 Medium Leather, 24
# Elixir of Minor Agility and 321 Heavy Leather.
# 150-225: recipes 5s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 7g 87s; gather or buy 22 Heavy
# Hide and 373 Thick Leather.
# 225-300: recipes 3g 40s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 44g 90s; gather or buy 1029
# Rugged Leather and 430 Runecloth.
#
# Data: recipes, colours and reagents from the Forever client's tables; trainer learn skills and
# prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists (they reach skill 50-150); vendors, stock and drops
# from data/forever. Materials are valued at about four times their vendor sell price (cloth and
# leather by the square root of it, hides four times higher; tools/lib/professions/materials.js) to
# rank recipes against each other, never as a price forecast.
# ASSUMED: learn skills of Barbaric Shoulders 150, Nightscape Headband 180, Nightscape Pants 210 and
# Rugged Armor Kit 225 (no sniffed Forever list teaches them: Classic's trainer skill moved as far
# as Forever moved the recipe's colours, which the sniffed lists bear out on 126 of 129 recipes).
# In-game check: the skill the trainer asks; their prices are not in the data.
# ASSUMED: rank level gates Expert 20 and Artisan 35 (Classic's; Forever's sniffed lists ask level 1
# for Apprentice and 10 for Journeyman). In-game check: the level each trainer asks.
# ASSUMED: Rugged Leather and Rugged Armor Kit are taught only by the Artisan trainers, Drakk
# Stonehand and Hahrana Ironhide (Classic's trainer lists; Forever's sniffed lists stop at 150).
# In-game check: whether Telonis or Una teach them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice (1-75)
section Leatherworking 1-75

step Learn Leatherworking
  tip Apprentice Leatherworking lets you craft up to 75 for 10c, at any character level. Not every Leatherworking trainer teaches it: Alliance Adele Fielder (Elwynn Forest), Darianna (Darnassus), Emerii Tallgust (Zephras Isle), Gretta Finespindle (Ironforge), Indari Sunseam (Zephras Isle), Nadyia Maneweaver (Teldrassil) and Randal Worth (Stormwind City); Horde Chaw Stronghide (Mulgore), Dan Golthas (Undercity), Emerii Tallgust (Zephras Isle), Indari Sunseam (Zephras Isle), Kamari (Orgrimmar), Mak (Thunder Bluff) and Shelene Rhobart (Tirisfal Glades). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Pair it with Skinning: Light Leather comes from the beasts of every starting zone. Coarse Thread and Salt are sold by leatherworking and trade supplies vendors. 1-75 takes about 1s 50c of recipes and 5s of vendor goods, plus 349 Light Leather to gather or buy.
  train Leatherworking Apprentice
  skill Leatherworking 1

step Leatherworking 1-75: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 50 Coarse Thread (5s); about 5s in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero, Edna Mullby and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya, Felika and Shimra).
  buy 2320 x50 nearest

